#reason skills/lantern-setup/scripts/prguide.mjs The guide needs one place that owns its limits, its record grammar and the check that every hunk belongs to one step.
#reason src/main/lantern-guide-parse.ts Gives the app the same strict reading of guide lines as the skill, so a guide means one thing everywhere
#reason src/renderer/lantern-guide.css Gives the Guide view its quiet look from existing theme variables.
#reason src/renderer/lib/lanternguide.ts Keeps the switch rules and the choice of rows a step owns apart from the DOM.
#reason src/renderer/lib/lanternguideview.ts Draws the guide as a short tour with its own state for the session.
#reason test/e2e/pr-review-guide.spec.ts Proves the guide opens, steps, folds, toggles and hands back to Files.
#reason test/helpers/lantern-guide-cases.ts Holds the guide cases and their expected messages so the parity test stays short
#reason test/lantern-guide-view.test.ts Pins row selection, the switch rules and the view behaviour without a browser.
#reason test/lantern-pr-guide.test.ts Pins the round trip, each limit and the missed and doubled hunk reports before later items build on them.
#reason test/lantern-sync-guide.test.ts Pins write, keep, clear, adopt and the red and green coverage cases.
#reason package.json Lists the new guide spec in the pull request review e2e script.
#reason scripts/e2e-delegate/README.md The check table must name the guide flag and the panel guide check
#reason scripts/e2e-delegate/checks.mjs The e2e checks must fail a delegate run whose record has no guide
#reason scripts/e2e-delegate/verify.mjs The branch verify in the e2e run must pass --require-guide like the delegate does
#reason scripts/esbuild.mjs Copies the new Guide stylesheet into the build.
#reason scripts/pr-review-demo.mjs Opens the demo on its guide so the tour can be looked at by hand.
#reason scripts/skill-test/fake-agent.mjs The fake delegate needs a valid guide, and a mode without one, to test the gate offline
#reason scripts/skill-test/run.mjs The no-guide fake must be selectable from the command line and documented in usage
#reason skills/lantern-delegate-complex/SKILL.md Keeps its description of what the heavy delegate records in step with the protocol
#reason skills/lantern-delegate/SKILL.md The orchestrator gate must require the guide and know which guides go back
#reason skills/lantern-delegate/protocol.md Delegates must write and record a guide so no PR ships without a reader's path through it
#reason skills/lantern-delegate/scripts/permissions.mjs An unattended delegate needs permission to edit its guide file
#reason skills/lantern-setup/references/format.md The guide section named the sync wiring as a later item; it now says what verify checks.
#reason skills/lantern-setup/scripts/prs.mjs A malformed guide has to fail a record the way a malformed flow does, so the reader never shows a broken guide.
#reason skills/lantern-sync/SKILL.md The guide scratch path is now named, so the old note that it is open is wrong
#reason skills/lantern-sync/scripts/sync.mjs Gates a delegate's guide like its flow: written by pr, hunk coverage checked from git by verify.
#reason src/main/lantern-local.ts Carries the guide of a local branch record onto its comparison like the flow
#reason src/main/lantern-pr-parse.ts Collects the guide lines of a record and keeps a bad guide from breaking the rest of it
#reason src/main/lantern-prs.ts Carries the parsed guide from a PR record onto the PR the map shows
#reason src/main/lantern-types.ts Defines the guide shape the review screen will read, with guideError beside it like flowError
#reason src/renderer/lantern.css Lets the Guide reuse the review diff colours instead of copying them.
#reason src/renderer/lib/lanternmacroview.ts Adds the Guide button to the view strip next to Files, Macro and Flow.
#reason src/renderer/lib/lanternprpanel.ts Lets the guide keep the header card in the left pane without the file list.
#reason src/renderer/lib/lanternview.ts Hosts the Guide like Flow and opens on it when the record has one.
#reason src/renderer/workspace.html Loads the Guide stylesheet in the app.
#reason test/e2e/app/index.html Loads the Guide stylesheet in the harness.
#reason test/e2e/app/main.cjs Passes the guide switch from the environment to the harness page.
#reason test/e2e/app/renderer.ts Attaches the demo guide only on request so other specs keep opening in Files.
#reason test/fixtures/graph/pr-review-demo.ts Gives the demo pull request a realistic five-step guide.
#reason test/lantern-delegate-delivery-flow.test.ts Proves the offline run is red without a guide, and that verify carries the new flag
#reason test/lantern-pr-parity.test.ts Fails when the app and the skill read a guide differently or the mirrored limits drift
#story Reading a pull request as a guide
#step actor A reviewer
#step action opens a pull request in Lantern
#step subject the review screen
#file src/renderer/lib/lanternguideview.ts
#below interaction reads it step by step with J and K and ticks steps off
#file src/renderer/lib/lanternguide.ts
#below consequence a list of files in review order => a few steps in reading order with only their own hunks
#story A delegate hands over its pull request
#step actor A Lantern delegate
#step action records its pull request
#step subject the guide for that change
#file skills/lantern-delegate/protocol.md
#file skills/lantern-sync/scripts/sync.mjs
#below consequence a record with reasons, order and flow => the same record cannot pass the gate without a guide covering every hunk
#guide A pull request reads as ordered steps with their own hunks, and every Lantern delegate must write that guide.
#risk medium Changes the delegate gate every run passes and adds a new mode to the review screen.
#gstep careful The guide grammar and its checks
#gwhy The record format every other step builds on: the guide lines, their limits and the hunk coverage check.
